  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(x)=\\frac{\\sin ^{-1}(x-3)}{\\sqrt{9-x^{2}}}$ is defined\r\n\r\nif (i) $-1 \\leq x-3 \\leq 1 \\Rightarrow 2 \\leq x \\leq 4$ and\r\n\r\n(ii) $9-x^{2}>0 \\Rightarrow-3<x<3$\r\n\r\nTaking common solution of (i) and (ii), we get $2 \\leq x<3$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore$ Domain $=[2,3)$"
  }
}